 6. 👀 Witkoff meets powerful UAE official 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Vessels sit near the Strait of Hormuz along the coast of Oman this week. Photo: Reuters White House envoy Steve Witkoff met last weekend with the national security adviser of the United Arab Emirates to discuss next steps on Iran, Axios' Barak Ravid writes. 

 Witkoff met with Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed Al Nahyan (TBZ) on the Mediterranean island of Sardinia. Why it matters: The talks, which weren't announced by the White House and haven't been reported until now, took place amid the Trump administration's push to reopen the Strait of Hormuz while choking Iran economically. 

 The UAE has been the key partner in the U.S.-led operation to reopen and guide oil tankers through the strait. Keep reading . 

 
 
