 7. 🏛️ Leadership power play fuels Dem infighting 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Michael M. Santiago/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 House Democratic leaders are trying to flex some muscle this week after two members defected on a key procedural vote. It's stoking fury among members across the political spectrum, Axios' Andrew Solender writes. 

 Why it matters: The blowup offers a preview of the chaos that party leaders could face in January if they take back the House majority. At the same time, an effort to give House Democratic leaders more tools to keep their members in line next year is falling flat among rank-and-file members.

 "It'll be dead by next week," predicted one senior House Democrat, speaking to Axios on the condition of anonymity to comment candidly on the maneuver. 🔭 Zoom in: Reps. Jared Golden (D-Maine) and Marie Gluesenkamp Perez (D-Wash.) angered fellow Democrats on Tuesday by helping Republicans pass a rule, or procedural measure.

 Some members have suggested kicking both members off their committees, or at least removing Gluesenkamp Perez from the powerful House Appropriations Committee. Others have pitched a broader change to caucus rules requiring members to show up to key votes, stick with party leadership on rule votes and pay their dues to the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee. Keep reading . 

 
 
